From: lindsayrpiper <lindsay.piper@sentry.io>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 21:07:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add web build and GitHub Pages deployment

QuarterTicker now ships as a static website in addition to the Electron app,
reusing the same renderer and quarter math. The only difference is config
storage: Electron IPC on desktop, localStorage in the browser.

- src/web-api.ts: localStorage-backed config bridge matching the preload shape
- src/web-entry.ts: installs the web bridge, then loads the shared renderer
- npm run build:web: bundles a self-contained static site into site/
- .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml: builds site/ and publishes to GitHub
  Pages on every push to main
- README: document the web version and one-time Pages setup

